### 3. The Pin-Change Interrupt False-Firing
**Pattern seen:**
AVR PCINT fires on ANY pin change, often triggered by MOSFET EMI:
```c
ISR(PCINT0_vect) {
    // Fire immediately!
}
// Problem: MOSFET commutation causes spurious edge on piezo pin
```
**Pattern people fix:**
```c
ISR(PCINT0_vect) {
    uint16_t pins_changed = PINC | PCMSK0;   // Get which
    if (pins_changed & PIN_CHANGE_TRIGGER) { // Only trigger pin
        trigger_pending = 1;                  // Buffer pulse
    }
}
```

### 4. Timer Capture vs Interrupt Resolution Mismatch
Pitfall: Using Timer Compare for time-critical >=10µs pulse.
**Pitfall pattern:**
```c
// Timer overflow at 2ms resolution (8-bit @16MHz)
if ((millis % 2000) < 15) {  // Too coarse!
    fire_matches();          // Window tolerance too low
}
```
**Quick fix:**
```c
